/-!
# PairIntent open-runtime classical no-section

Every local revised visit has the same exact classical Bool current `true`,
while the authoritative erasure of the same named runtime state remembers its
generated temporal history.  The true classical fibre therefore contains an
injective copy of every finite runtime depth.

Raw Bool reconstructors remain an inhabited ordinary function language.  The
no-go is generated by two concrete runtime states, not by defining syntax as a
failure fibre: depth zero and depth one share the same classical current but
carry different authoritative occurrences.
-/

set_option autoImplicit false

namespace SaturationMonoid
